  {
    id: 165,
    label: "正論解 41.4",
    title: { zh: "正論解 41.4", en: "Shusun Zhaozi, Shuxiang, and Straight Judgment" },
    text: {
      zh: `楚靈王若能如是，豈期辱於幹溪？子革之非左史，所以風也。稱詩以諫，順哉。」叔孫穆子，避難奔齊。宿於庚宗之邑，庚宗寡婦通焉而生牛。穆子返魯，以牛為內豎，相家。牛讒叔孫二人，殺之。叔孫有病，牛不通其饋，不食而死。牛遂輔叔孫庶子昭，而立之。昭子既立朝，其家眾曰：「豎牛禍叔孫氏，使亂大從。殺適立庶，又被其邑，以求舍罪。罪莫大焉，必速殺之。」遂殺豎牛。孔子曰：「叔孫昭子不勞，不可能也。周任有言曰：『為政者：不賞私勞，不罰私怨。』詩云：『有覺德行，四國順之。』昭子有焉。」晉邢侯與雍子爭田，叔魚攝理，罪在雍子。雍子納其女於叔魚，叔魚弊獄邢侯。邢侯怒殺叔魚與雍子於朝。韓宣子問罪於叔向。叔向曰：「三奸同坐，施生戮死可也。雍子自知其罪，而賂以置直鮒也，鬻獄邢侯專殺其罪一也。己惡而掠美為昏，貪以敗官為默，殺人不忌為賊。夏書曰：『昏、默、賊，殺。咎陶之刑也。』請從之。」乃施邢侯，而屍雍子、叔魚於市。孔子曰：「叔向，古之遺直也。治國制刑，不隱於親。`,
      en: `Shusun Muz fleeing to Qi sired Niu with a widow; Niu slandered and killed two uncles, blocked feeding when Muz was ill — Muz starved. Niu installed a younger son. When Zhaozi took court, the clan said kill the chamberlain Niu for great disorder. They killed Niu. Confucius: "Shusun Zhaozi without labor could not succeed. Zhou Ren said: rulers do not reward private labor, do not punish private grudges."

Jin Xing Hou and Yongzi disputed land; Shuyu judged for Yongzi who bribed with his daughter; Xing Hou killed Shuyu and Yongzi in court. Han Xuanzi asked Shuxiang's guilt. Shuxiang said three wicked together — bribery, perverting judgment, murder — apply Xia punishments. Xing Hou executed; Yongzi and Shuyu exposed in market. Confucius: "Shuxiang, ancient straight remnant — governing state and making punishments, not hiding from kin."`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: "孔子接著說：楚靈王若能做到克己復禮，哪裡會在乾溪受辱？子革批評左史，正是為了諷勸；引用詩句來進諫，可謂順當。叔孫穆子避難逃到齊國，住在庚宗之邑，與庚宗寡婦私通而生下豎牛。穆子返回魯國後，以豎牛為內豎、掌管家政；豎牛讒害叔孫氏的兩個人並加以殺害。叔孫生病時，豎牛不通飲食給他，終於餓死；豎牛於是輔佐叔孫的庶子昭，立他為後。昭子既已立朝，家眾說：豎牛禍害叔孫氏，擾亂大宗，殺嫡立庶，又侵佔城邑來求免罪，罪沒有比這更大的，必須立刻殺掉他——於是殺了豎牛。孔子說：叔孫昭子若不費心力，是不可能做到的。周任有言：執政的人不賞私人功勞，不罰私人怨恨。《詩》云「有正直的德行，四方之國都順從」——昭子正有這樣的德行。晉國邢侯與雍子爭田，叔魚代理審理，罪過本在雍子；雍子把女兒送給叔魚，叔魚便枉法判決邢侯有罪。邢侯憤怒，在朝廷上殺了叔魚與雍子。韓宣子向叔向詢問當如何定罪。叔向說：三個奸人罪責相同，對活著的施加刑罰、對死了的陳屍都可以——雍子自知有罪卻用賄賂來收買正直，叔魚出賣獄訟，邢侯專擅殺人，罪過是一樣的。自己醜惡卻掠取美名叫做昏，貪婪而敗壞官職叫做墨，殺人毫無忌憚叫做賊；《夏書》說昏、墨、賊，殺——這是皋陶的刑罰。請依此辦理。於是把邢侯處死，又把雍子、叔魚陳屍於市。孔子說：叔向真是古代遺留下來的正直之人——治理國家、制定刑罰，不因為是親人就加以隱瞞。豎牛之獄見昭子能去賊而不牽私；邢侯之獄見叔向把賄、鬻獄、專殺併為一罪，雖叔魚是其親亦不隱——孔子前後稱「有覺德行」與「古之遺直」，把「不賞私勞、不罰私怨」和「不隱於親」立為正論的刑政標準。",
      en: "Confucius continues: had King Ling of Chu been able to restrain himself and return to ritual, would he have met shame at Ganxi? Zige's criticizing the left historian was to admonish by wind; citing poetry to remonstrate was compliant indeed. Shusun Muzi, fleeing trouble to Qi, lodged at Gengzong and with a widow there sired the chamberlain Niu. Returning to Lu he made Niu inner attendant over the household; Niu slandered and killed two of the Shusun line. When Muzi fell ill, Niu blocked his food until he starved; Niu then installed the younger son Zhao. Once Zhaozi took court, the clan said Niu had ruined the house — disordering the main line, killing the rightful heir, installing the younger, and seizing towns to buy off guilt — greatest crime; they must kill him quickly — and so they did. Confucius said: Shusun Zhaozi without labor could not have succeeded. Zhou Ren said: rulers do not reward private labor or punish private grudges. The Odes: \"Upright virtue — the four states follow it\" — Zhaozi had this. In Jin, Xing Hou and Yongzi disputed land; Shuyu judged as deputy, guilt with Yongzi; Yongzi bribed Shuyu with his daughter, and Shuyu perverted the case against Xing Hou. Xing Hou angrily killed Shuyu and Yongzi in court. Han Xuanzi asked Shuxiang how to assign guilt. Shuxiang said three wicked share the same seat — punish the living and expose the dead: Yongzi knew his guilt and bribed to bend the straight; Shuyu sold the case; Xing Hou murdered on his own — one crime. Evil that steals praise is hun; greed that ruins office is mo; killing without dread is thief; the Xia Documents say hun, mo, and thief are killed — Gaoyao's punishments. Follow them. So Xing Hou was executed and Yongzi and Shuyu exposed in the market. Confucius said: Shuxiang is an ancient remnant of straightness — governing the state and making punishments, he did not hide because of kinship. The Niu case shows Zhaozi removing a villain without private entanglement; the Xing Hou case shows Shuxiang treating bribery, selling judgment, and murder as one crime, not hiding even though Shuyu was kin — Confucius praises upright virtue and ancient straightness, setting \"no private rewards or grudges\" and \"no concealment for kin\" as the penal standard of right discourse."
    },
    application: {
      zh: "公义不因私劳、私怨而偏移；至親犯法，亦不可隐。\n<br /><b>建議：若你主持纠纷，先寫下與双方私交程度，並声明將依事证而非关系裁决。</b>",
      en: "Public justice ignores private favors and grudges; even kin must not be hidden in judgment.\n<br /><b>Suggestion: When mediating, note your ties to each party and state you will decide on evidence, not relation.</b>"
    }
  },
  {
    id: 166,
    label: "正論解 41.5",
    title: { zh: "正論解 41.5", en: "Zichan on the Village School and Tribute at Pingqiu" },
    text: {
      zh: `三數叔魚之罪，不為末。或曰義，可謂直矣。平丘之會，數其賄也。以寬衛國，晉不為暴；歸魯季孫，稱其詐也。以寬魯國，晉不為虐；邢侯之獄，言其貪也，以正刑書，晉不為頗。三言而除三惡，加三利，殺親益榮，由義也夫。」鄭有鄉校。鄉校之士，非論執政，鬷明欲毀鄉校。子產曰：「何以毀為也？夫人朝夕退而遊焉，以議執政之善否。其所善者，吾則行之；其所否者，吾則改之。若之何其毀也？我聞忠言以損怨，不聞立威以防怨。防怨，猶防水也。大決所犯，傷人必多，吾弗克救也。不如小決使導之，不如吾所聞而藥之。」孔子聞是言也，曰：「吾以是觀之，人謂子產不仁，吾不信也。」晉平公會諸侯於平丘。齊侯及盟，鄭子產爭貢賦之所承，曰：「昔日天子班貢輕重，以列尊卑。貢，周之制也。卑而貢重者甸服，鄭伯，男南也。而使從公侯之貢懼弗給也。敢以為請。」自日中爭之，以至於昏。晉人許之。孔子曰：「子產於是行也，是以為國基也。詩云：『樂只君子，邦家之基。』子產，君子之於樂者。`,
      en: `At Pingqiu assembly Zichan argued tribute shares from midday to dusk — Jin consented. Confucius: "Zichan on this journey is the state's foundation. The Odes: 'Happy the gentleman — foundation of clan and state.'"

Zheng had village schools where people debated policy. Zichan refused to destroy them: "Morning and evening they gather and judge governance good or bad — what they approve I do; what they reject I change. I hear loyal words reduce resentment — not building authority to prevent resentment. Blocking resentment is like blocking water — a great breach hurts many. Better a small outlet and medicine for what I hear." Confucius: "From this I see — whoever says Zichan lacks benevolence, I do not believe."`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: "孔子稱贊叔向三次數落叔魚的罪過都不肯從輕，有人說這就是義，可稱得上正直了：在平丘之會上指出他受賄，藉此寬緩衛國而使晉不至於暴虐；送還魯國的季孫時指出他欺詐，藉此寬緩魯國而使晉不至於酷虐；在邢侯之獄中指出他貪婪，藉此端正刑書而使晉不至於偏頗——三句話除去三樣惡、加上三樣利，即使殺了親人卻更增榮耀，正是由於義啊。鄭國有鄉校，鄉校裡的士人議論執政的得失，鬷明想拆毀鄉校。子產說：為什麼要拆？人們早晚退朝後到那裡遊聚，議論執政的好壞；他們稱贊的，我就施行；他們否定的，我就改正——怎麼能拆呢？我聽說用忠言減少怨恨，沒聽說靠立威來防堵怨恨。防堵怨恨如同防堵洪水：一旦大決口，傷人必定很多，我也無法挽救；不如開小口加以疏導，不如把我所聽到的當作治病的藥石。孔子聽到這番話，說：我從這件事來看，有人說子產不仁，我不相信。晉平公在平丘會盟諸侯，齊侯也參與盟約；鄭國子產爭執貢賦應當承擔多少，說：從前天子按尊卑排列貢賦輕重，貢本是周的制度；地位低而貢重的是甸服，鄭伯屬於男服，卻要我們按公侯的貢額繳納，恐怕供應不起——斗膽請求調整。從正午爭論到黃昏，晉人終於答應。孔子說：子產在這次行動中，正是為國家奠定根基。《詩》云「快樂啊君子，是邦家的根基」——子產，正是君子中能得此樂的人。叔向三言除三惡之後，本文重心转到子產：不毀鄉校，是以小決導怨、以所聞為藥；平丘爭貢自日中至昏，是為邦家爭得可負擔的制度。孔子先斷「人謂子產不仁，吾不信」，再斷「是以為國基」，把納諫與爭制都視為仁政的根基。",
      en: "Confucius praises Shuxiang for thrice numbering Shuyu's crimes without making light of them — some call it righteousness; it may be called straightness. At the Pingqiu assembly he numbered bribery, easing Wei so Jin was not violent; returning Ji Sun of Lu he named deceit, easing Lu so Jin was not cruel; in the Xing Hou case he spoke of greed, rectifying the penal code so Jin was not partial — three speeches removed three evils and added three benefits; killing kin yet increasing honor comes from righteousness. Zheng had village schools where gentlemen debated the rulers' successes and failures; Zong Ming wished to destroy them. Zichan asked why: morning and evening people withdraw and gather there to judge governance good or bad — what they approve I do; what they reject I change — how destroy that? I hear loyal words reduce resentment, not building authority to block it. Blocking resentment is like blocking floodwaters: a great breach hurts many and I cannot save them; better a small outlet to guide it, better to take what I hear as medicine. Confucius heard this and said: from this I see — whoever says Zichan lacks benevolence, I do not believe. At Pingqiu Duke Ping of Jin met the lords; Qi joined the covenant. Zichan of Zheng disputed the tribute share: formerly the Son of Heaven graded tribute by rank; tribute is Zhou's system; heavy tribute on the lowly was for the royal domain, while Zheng is a nan-rank lord yet made to follow dukes' and marquises' dues — he feared they could not supply it. He argued from midday to dusk; Jin consented. Confucius said: on this journey Zichan is laying the state's foundation. The Odes: \"Happy the gentleman — foundation of clan and state\" — Zichan is a gentleman who finds that joy. After Shuxiang's three speeches remove three evils, the focus turns to Zichan: refusing to destroy village schools is guiding resentment by a small outlet and taking what he hears as medicine; disputing tribute at Pingqiu from noon to dusk wins a bearable system for the state. Confucius first denies that Zichan lacks benevolence, then calls him the state's foundation — taking loyal criticism and institutional contention alike as the root of humane rule."
    },
    application: {
      zh: "防怨如防水，宜疏導；允許批评的制度，往往比壓服更稳固。\n<br /><b>建議：在團隊設一个固定「可否反馈」渠道（短會或匿名），本周讀一條並回應是否采纳。</b>",
      en: "Blocking resentment like water fails; channels for loyal criticism stabilize rule.\n<br /><b>Suggestion: Open one fixed feedback channel this week; read one item and say whether you will act on it.</b>"
    }
  },
  {
    id: 167,
    label: "正論解 41.6",
    title: { zh: "正論解 41.6", en: "Broad and Stern Governance; Tyranny Worse Than Tigers" },
    text: {
      zh: `且曰合諸侯而藝貢事，禮也。」鄭子產有疾，謂子太叔曰：「我死，子必為政。唯有德者能以寬服民，其次莫如猛。夫火烈民望而畏之，故鮮死焉；水濡弱，民狎而翫之，則多死焉。故寬難。」子產卒，子太叔為政。不忍猛而寬，鄭國多掠盜。太叔悔之曰：「吾早從夫子，必不及此。」孔子聞之曰：「善哉！政寬則民慢，慢則糾於猛。猛則民殘，民殘則施之以寬。寬以濟猛，猛以濟寬，寬猛相濟，政是以和。詩曰：『民亦勞止，汔可小康。惠此中國，以綏四方。』施之以寬，毋縱詭隨。以謹無良，式遏寇虐，慘不畏明，糾之以猛也。柔遠能邇，以定我王，平之以和也。」又曰：「不競不絿，不剛不柔。布政優優，百祿是遒。和之至也。」子產之卒也，孔子聞之，出涕曰：「古之遺愛。」孔子適齊，過泰山之側，有婦人哭於野者而哀。夫子式而聽之曰：「此哀一似重有憂者。」使子貢問之。而曰：「昔舅死於虎，吾夫又死焉，今吾子又死焉。」子貢曰：「何不去乎？」婦人曰：「無苛政。」子貢以告孔子。子曰：「小子識之，苛政猛於暴虎。」`,
      en: `Zichan ill told successor Taishu: only the virtuous can govern with breadth; next best is sternness — fire fierce, people fear, few die; water soft, people play, many die — therefore breadth is hard. After Zichan died Taishu was lenient; bandits multiplied. Taishu regretted not heeding. Confucius praised the doctrine: breadth then sternness, sternness then breadth — government harmonizes. Citing Odes on ease and restraint.

Confucius passing Mount Tai heard a woman weep — husband, son, and father-in-law all killed by tigers. Asked why not leave — "No harsh government." Confucius: "Remember — harsh government is fiercer than wild tigers."`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: "孔子又說：會合諸侯而規範貢事，正是合於禮。鄭國子產病重，對子太叔說：我死之後，你必定執政。只有有德的人能用寬厚使百姓服從，其次就不如用猛政。火勢猛烈，百姓望而生畏，所以很少燒死；水勢柔弱，百姓輕慢玩弄，反而多有淹死——所以寬政其實很難。子產去世，子太叔執政，不忍用猛而專用寬，鄭國多有搶劫盜賊。太叔後悔說：我若早聽從夫子，必不至於此。孔子聽說後稱贊：說得好啊！政寬則民怠慢，怠慢就要用猛來糾正；猛則民受殘害，民殘就要再用寬來緩和。寬用來濟猛，猛用來濟寬，寬猛相互補充，政治因此和諧。他又引《詩》說百姓勞苦已極、但求小康，施惠中原以安定四方——這是施寬；不要放縱詭詐隨和之人，謹防不良，遏止寇虐——這是糾猛；安撫遠人、親睦近人來安定王室——這是平和。又說為政不爭競、不急躁，不偏剛、不偏柔，布政優游寬和——這是和的極致。子產去世時，孔子聽說後流淚說：這是古代遺留下來的仁愛。孔子前往齊國，經過泰山旁邊，有婦人在野外哭得十分哀痛。夫子憑軾而聽，說這哀痛好像重重憂傷疊加，派子貢去問。婦人說：從前公公死於虎口，我丈夫又死於虎，如今兒子又死於虎。子貢問為什麼不離開這裡，婦人說：因為這裡沒有苛政。子貢告訴孔子，孔子說：弟子們記住——苛政比兇猛的老虎還可怕。子產臨終授「寬難於猛」，太叔寬而盜起，孔子乃總結寬猛相濟、並以《詩》之小康、謹無良、柔遠能邇相印證；及聞子產卒而稱「古之遺愛」，再以泰山婦人「無苛政」寧死於虎的故事，把「猛」從必要的刑政一轉，警戒「苛」比虎更可怕。",
      en: "Confucius also said that assembling the feudal lords and regulating tribute is ritual. Ill, Zichan told Taishu: when I die you must govern. Only the virtuous can win the people by breadth; next best is sternness. Fire is fierce — people look and fear, so few die by it; water is soft — people play with it, so many die — therefore breadth is hard. After Zichan died Taishu could not bear sternness and governed with breadth; bandits multiplied in Zheng. Taishu regretted: had I followed the Master earlier, I would not have come to this. Confucius heard and praised: well said! When government is broad the people grow slack, and slackness is corrected by sternness; when stern, the people are harmed, and harm is eased by breadth. Breadth aiding sternness and sternness aiding breadth — government is thereby harmonious. He cited the Odes on easing the people's toil toward modest ease and securing the center to quiet the four quarters — that is applying breadth; on not indulging crafty followers and checking violence — that is correcting with sternness; on gentling the far and enabling the near to settle the king — that is peace. Again: neither straining nor rushing, neither hard nor soft, government ample and easy — the utmost of harmony. At Zichan's death Confucius wept: an ancient remnant of love. Passing Mount Tai toward Qi he heard a woman weep bitterly in the wilds; standing against the chariot bar he listened and said this grief seemed to bear layered sorrow. He sent Zigong to ask. She said: formerly my husband's father died by a tiger, then my husband, now my son. Asked why she did not leave: there is no harsh government here. Zigong reported; Confucius said: remember, youths — harsh government is fiercer than a wild tiger. Zichan's dying charge that breadth is harder than sternness, Taishu's lenience breeding bandits, and Confucius's doctrine of breadth and sternness aiding each other are sealed by Odes on modest ease, checking the wicked, and gentling far and near; weeping for Zichan as an ancient remnant of love, he then turns — through the Mount Tai woman who stays among tigers because there is no harsh government — from necessary sternness to the warning that tyranny is fiercer than the tiger."
    },
    application: {
      zh: "政宽則慢，猛則残，須相濟；百姓怕的有時不是虎，而是不可預测的苛法。\n<br /><b>建議：檢視你定的一條规則：是否清晰可遵？若多数人不解而受罚，即屬「苛政」之微。</b>",
      en: "Lenience slackens, harshness harms — they must alternate; people sometimes fear arbitrary rules more than tigers.\n<br /><b>Suggestion: Review one rule you enforce — is it clear? If many fail without understanding, it approaches tyranny.</b>"
    }
  },
  {
    id: 168,
    label: "正論解 41.7",
    title: { zh: "正論解 41.7", en: "Wei Xu's Appointments, Casting Law in Bronze, and King Zhao" },
    text: {
      zh: `晉魏獻子為政，分祁氏及羊舌氏之田，荀櫟滅，以賞諸大夫，及其子成，皆以賢舉也。又將賈辛曰：「今汝有力於王室，吾是以舉汝。行乎敬之哉，毋墮乃力。」孔子聞之曰：「魏子之舉也，近不失親，遠不失舉，可謂美矣。」又聞其命賈辛以為忠。詩云：「永言配命，自求多福。」忠也。魏子之舉也，義其命也。忠其長有後於晉國乎？趙簡子賦晉國一鼓鐘，以鑄刑鼎，著範宣子所為刑書。孔子曰：「晉其亡乎？失其度矣。夫晉國將守唐叔之所受法度，以經緯其民者也。卿大夫以序守之，民是以能遵其道而守其業，貴賤不愆，所謂度也。文公是以作執秩之官，為被廬之法，以為盟主。今棄此度也，而為刑鼎，銘在鼎矣，何以尊貴？何業之守也？貴賤無序，何以為國？且夫宣子之刑，夷之搜也，晉國亂制，若之何其為法乎。」楚昭王有疾，卜曰：「河神為祟。」王弗祭，大夫請祭諸郊。王曰：「三代命祀，祭不越望。江漢沮漳，楚之望也。禍福之至，不是過乎？不谷雖不德，河非所獲罪也。」遂不祭。孔子曰：「楚昭王知大道矣。`,
      en: `Wei Xianzi divided Qi and Yangshe lands, rewarding worthy officers including his son — telling Jia Xin to stay reverent. Confucius praised near not losing kin, far not losing worth.

Zhao Jianzi cast bell into a punishment tripod inscribing Fan Xuanzi's penal code. Confucius: "Jin will perish — lost its measure. Nobles and officers kept degrees so people followed occupations — now law is on bronze — how maintain rank and duty?"

Chu King Zhao ill — divination blamed the river god; he refused sacrifice beyond Chu rivers — "Fortune and disaster are not there." Confucius: "King Zhao knew the great Way — fitting he kept his state."`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: "晉國魏獻子執政，分配祁氏與羊舌氏的田地；荀櫟被滅之後，把那些田賞給諸位大夫以及自己的兒子魏成，都是因為賢能而舉用。他又對賈辛說：如今你有功於王室，我因此舉用你——去就任時要敬慎啊，不要讓你的力氣墮廢。孔子聽說後說：魏子的舉用，對近處不因私而失親，對遠處不因疏而漏舉，可稱美好了。又聽說他任命賈辛時寄託的是忠。《詩》云「永遠配合天命，自己求取多福」——這就是忠。魏子的舉用合於義，他的任命合於忠，他恐怕會長遠在晉國有後嗣吧？趙簡子向晉國徵收一鼓的鐵，用來鑄造刑鼎，把範宣子所訂的刑書鑄在上面。孔子說：晉國大概要滅亡了吧？它失去法度了。晉國本應遵守唐叔所受的法度來經緯治理百姓；卿大夫按位序守住它，百姓因此能遵循正道、守住本業，貴賤都不逾越，這就是所謂的「度」。文公因此設立執秩之官、制定被廬之法，才成為盟主。如今拋棄這法度而鑄刑鼎，條文已銘在鼎上，還憑什麼尊貴？還守什麼本業？貴賤失去秩序，還憑什麼立國？況且宣子的刑罰，本出於夷地閱兵時的亂制，晉國紊亂的制度，又怎能當作法呢？楚昭王生病，占卜說是河神作祟。昭王不肯祭祀；大夫請在郊外祭祀。昭王說：三代規定的祭祀，祭不超出本國的望祀——長江、漢水、沮水、漳水，才是楚的望；禍福到來，難道會超出這些嗎？我雖然無德，卻不是獲罪於黄河之神。於是不祭。孔子說：楚昭王懂得大道了。魏獻子舉人近不失親、遠不失舉，又忠言囑賈辛；相對地，趙簡子鑄刑鼎棄唐叔法度與被廬之制，孔子憂晉失「度」；楚昭王則堅守「祭不越望」，不以河神之卜亂楚之祀典——舉賢、守度、知祀，三者都是正論裡的「大道」。",
      en: "Wei Xianzi governing Jin divided the fields of the Qi and Yangshe clans; after Xun Li was destroyed he rewarded those fields to the great officers and to his own son Cheng — all chosen for worth. He also told Jia Xin: you have served the royal house with strength, therefore I raise you — go and revere it; do not let your strength fall. Confucius heard: Wei's appointments neither lose kin nearby nor lose the worthy afar — beautiful indeed. Hearing the charge to Jia Xin he called it loyalty. The Odes: \"Ever match the Mandate; seek much blessing yourself\" — loyalty. Wei's raising was righteous and his charge loyal — would he long have heirs in Jin? Zhao Jianzi levied a drum-measure of iron from Jin to cast a punishment tripod inscribed with Fan Xuanzi's penal code. Confucius said: will Jin perish? It has lost its measure. Jin was to keep the laws Tangshu received to order its people; ministers kept them by rank so people could follow the Way and guard their work — noble and base not in error: that is measure. Duke Wen made the office of ranks and the Beilu laws to be covenant leader. Now abandoning this measure for a punishment tripod — once law is on the bronze, how honor the noble? what occupation to guard? without order of ranks, how be a state? Moreover Xuanzi's punishments came from the disordered system of the Yi hunt — how make that law? Chu King Zhao was ill; divination blamed the river god. He would not sacrifice; officers asked for suburban sacrifice. The king said: the Three Dynasties' mandated rites do not sacrifice beyond the prospect — Jiang, Han, Ju, and Zhang are Chu's prospects; do fortune and disaster go beyond these? Though I lack virtue, the Yellow River is not where I have offended. So he did not sacrifice. Confucius said: King Zhao of Chu knew the great Way. Wei Xianzi raises men without losing kin nearby or worth afar, and charges Jia Xin with loyalty; by contrast Zhao Jianzi's punishment tripod abandons Tangshu's measure and the Beilu laws, and Confucius fears Jin has lost \"measure\"; King Zhao of Chu keeps sacrifices within Chu's own prospects and will not let a river-god omen scramble the rites — raising the worthy, keeping measure, and knowing sacrifice are all \"great Way\" within right discourse."
    },
    application: {
      zh: "舉才近不蔽親、遠不棄贤；法不可只铭於器而失禮之序；祭不在迷信，在知分。\n<br /><b>建議：做一次人事或规則决定時，分别問：是否任人唯親？是否只重條文轻情理？</b>",
      en: "Appoint without nepotism or neglect; law on bronze cannot replace ritual order; sacrifice is knowing limits, not superstition.\n<br /><b>Suggestion: In one personnel or policy choice, ask both: any favoritism? Any rule without humane context?</b>"
    }
  },
  {
    id: 169,
    label: "正論解 41.8",
    title: { zh: "正論解 41.8", en: "Confucius Declines Military Advice and Demands Punishment of Regicide" },
    text: {
      zh: `其不失國也，宜哉。夏書曰：『維彼陶唐，率彼天常，在此冀方。今失厥道，亂其紀綱，乃滅而亡。』」又曰：「允出茲在茲，由己率常可矣。」衛孔文子使太叔疾出其妻，而以其女妻之。疾誘其初妻之娣，為之立宮，與文子女，如二妻之禮。文子怒將攻之。孔子舍蘧伯玉之家，文子就而訪焉。孔子曰：「簠簋之事，則嘗聞學之矣。兵甲之事，未之聞也。」退而命駕而行曰：「鳥則擇木，木豈能擇鳥乎？」文子遽自止之曰：「圉也豈敢度其私哉？亦訪衛國之難也。」將止，會季康子問冉求之戰，冉求既對之，又曰：「夫子播之百姓，質諸鬼神，而無憾，用之則有名。」康子言於哀公，以幣迎孔子曰：「人之於冉求信之矣，將大用之。」齊陳恒弒其簡公。孔子聞之，三日沐浴而適朝，告於哀公曰：「陳恒弒其君，請伐之。」公弗許，三請。公曰：「魯為齊弱久矣。子之伐也，將若之何？」對曰：「陳恒弒其君，民之不與者半。以魯之眾，加齊之半，可克也。」公曰：「子告季氏。」孔子辭，退而告人曰：「以吾從大夫之後，吾不敢不告也。」`,
      en: `Wei Kong Wenzi's son-in-law Tai Shu Ji expelled his wife yet seduced her sister — Kong Wenzi would attack. Confucius lodging with Qu Bo Yu said he had heard of vessels but not of arms — drove away: "Birds choose trees — can trees choose birds?" Wenzi stopped, saying he sought counsel for Wei's trouble.

Chen Heng assassinated Duke Jian of Qi. Confucius bathed and went to court thrice asking Duke Ai to punish — refused as Lu is weak. Confucius said as follower of ministers he dared not fail to report — half Qi would not follow Heng; with Lu's multitude added, victory possible. The duke told him to tell Ji clan; Confucius declined and withdrew.`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: "孔子稱楚昭王知大道，其不失國也宜哉；並引《夏書》說陶唐氏遵循天常、在冀方之地，一旦失道亂紀便會滅亡；又說「允出茲在茲」，由自己率先遵循常道就可以了。衛國孔文子讓太叔疾休掉妻子，卻把自己的女兒嫁給他；太叔疾又引誘前妻的妹妹，為她另立宮室，與文子的女兒並行二妻之禮。文子大怒，準備攻打他。那時孔子住在蘧伯玉家，文子前來求問。孔子說：簠簋祭祀之事，我曾聽過也學過；兵甲攻戰之事，我沒有聽過。退下後命人駕車要走，說：鳥可以選擇樹木，樹木難道能選擇鳥嗎？文子急忙拦住他說：圉哪敢只為私怨打算？也是為衛國的危難來求教啊。正要留下時，恰逢季康子向冉求詢問戰事；冉求答完後又說：夫子把道理播於百姓、質正於鬼神而無所遺憾，任用他便會有名聲。康子告訴哀公，用幣帛迎接孔子，說：人們對冉求已經信任了，將要大大任用他。齊國陳恒弒殺簡公。孔子聽說後，沐浴三日然後上朝，告訴哀公：陳恒弒其君，請出兵討伐。哀公不許，孔子一連請求三次。哀公說：魯被齊削弱已經很久了，你要討伐，將怎麼辦？孔子對答：陳恒弒君，百姓不附和他的有一半；以魯國之眾加上齊國的一半，可以戰勝。哀公說：你去告訴季氏。孔子辭謝，退下後對人說：因為我曾跟從於大夫之列，我不敢不稟告。對孔文子，孔子以「未聞兵甲」拒為私鬥之謀主，並以「鳥擇木」示去就；對陳恒弒君，則沐浴三請伐齊，雖知魯弱、終被推給季氏，仍自稱「從大夫之後，不敢不告」——該拒的兵與該討的弒，分寸截然。",
      en: "Confucius said King Zhao of Chu knew the great Way — fitting that he did not lose his state — and cited the Xia Documents on Tao Tang following Heaven's constant in the Ji region: losing the Way and disordering the guidelines brings extinction; \"truly what goes out from here stays here\" — leading the constant from oneself is enough. In Wei, Kong Wenzi made Tai Shu Ji put away his wife and marry Kong's daughter; Ji then enticed his first wife's younger sister, built her a palace, and treated her with Kong's daughter as if two wives. Wenzi angrily would attack. Confucius was lodging with Qu Boyu; Wenzi came to consult. Confucius said he had heard and studied the affairs of sacrificial vessels, but not the affairs of arms. He withdrew, ordered the carriage, and said: birds choose trees — can trees choose birds? Wenzi hastily stopped him: how dare I measure only private ends? I also seek counsel for Wei's trouble. About to stay, Ji Kangzi asked Ran Qiu about war; Ran Qiu answered and added that the Master broadcasts among the people and verifies before ghosts and spirits without regret — use him and there will be renown. Kangzi told Duke Ai, who welcomed Confucius with gifts, saying people already trust Ran Qiu and will greatly use him. Chen Heng of Qi assassinated Duke Jian. Confucius heard, bathed three days, and went to court, telling Duke Ai: Chen Heng killed his lord — please attack. Refused, he asked thrice. The duke said Lu has long been weaker than Qi — what then of your attack? Confucius answered: half the people do not follow Chen Heng; with Lu's multitude added to half of Qi, we can overcome. The duke said tell the Ji clan. Confucius declined, withdrew, and told others: having followed among the great officers, I dared not fail to report. Toward Kong Wenzi, Confucius refuses to mastermind a private war — \"I have not heard of arms\" — and shows leave-taking with \"birds choose trees\"; toward Chen Heng's regicide he bathes and thrice petitions to attack Qi, and though Lu is weak and he is pushed toward the Ji clan, he still says that having followed among the great officers he dared not fail to report — the arms to refuse and the regicide to denounce are sharply distinct."
    },
    application: {
      zh: "越职之兵不贊；弑君之恶不可默然——明知不可為仍盡告知之责。\n<br /><b>建議：見明顯不义之事，即使無力改变，也完成一次正式反映或记錄，不留「未敢言」。</b>",
      en: "Do not aid private war; regicide demands voice — report even when success is unlikely.\n<br /><b>Suggestion: On clear injustice you cannot fix, still make one formal report or record — not silent complicity.</b>"
    }
  },
  {
    id: 170,
    label: "正論解 41.9",
    title: { zh: "正論解 41.9", en: "Mourning Protocol and Names Must Not Be Lent" },
    text: {
      zh: `子張問曰：「書云：『高宗三年不言，言乃雍。』有諸？」孔子曰：「胡為其不然也？古者天子崩，則世子委政於冢宰三年。成湯既沒，太甲聽於伊尹；武王既喪，成王聽於周公；其義一也。」衛孫桓子侵齊，遇敗焉。齊人乘之，執新築大夫，仲叔於奚以其眾救桓子，桓子乃免。衛人以邑賞仲叔於奚，於奚辭。請曲懸之樂，繁纓以朝。許之，書在三官。子路仕衛，見其故，以訪孔子。孔子曰：「惜也，不如多與之邑。惟器與名，不可以假人，君之所司，名以出信，信以守器，器以藏禮，禮以行義，義以生利，利以平民，政之大節也。若以假人，與人政也。政亡，則國家從之，不可止也。」公父文伯之母，紡績不解。文伯諫焉。其母曰：「古者王後親織玄紞，公侯之夫人加之纮綖，卿之內子為大帶，命婦成祭服，男女紡績，愆則有辟。聖王之制也，今我寡也，爾又在位，朝夕恪勤，猶恐忘先人之業，況有怠墮，其何以避辟？」孔子聞之曰：「弟子誌之：季氏之婦，可謂不過矣。」`,
      en: `Zizhang asked about "Gaozong three years without speech then harmonious" — Confucius explained heir delegates to chief minister three years — same for Taijia and Duke of Zhou.

Wei Sun Huanzi defeated by Qi; Zhongshu Yuxi saved him, refused fief, asked for suspended music and court tassels — granted, recorded in three offices. Zilu asked Confucius who said pity — better many fiefs. "Vessels and names cannot be lent — names issue trust, trust guards vessels, vessels store ritual, ritual carries righteousness — great node of government. Lending them gives away government; state follows to ruin."

Gongfu Wenbo's mother spun without cease; son remonstrated — she cited queens and officers' wives spinning, saying even widowed in office she must not slack. Confucius: "Ji clan's wife — cannot be surpassed."`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: "子張問：《書》裡說「高宗三年不說話，一說話便和諧順暢」，有這回事嗎？孔子說：為什麼會不是這樣呢？古代天子崩逝，世子把政事委託給冢宰三年。成湯去世後，太甲聽命於伊尹；武王去世後，成王聽命於周公——道理是一樣的。衛國孫桓子侵齊而戰敗，齊人乘勢抓住新築大夫；仲叔於奚率領部眾救了桓子，桓子纔得免難。衛人要用城邑賞賜仲叔於奚，於奚推辭，轉而請求享用曲懸之樂，並以繁纓之飾上朝；衛君答應了，還登記在三官的簿籍裡。子路在衛做官，見到這件事便去問孔子。孔子說：可惜啊，不如多給他一些城邑。只有禮器和名號不可以隨便借給別人——這是國君所執掌的：名號用來發出信用，信用用來守護禮器，禮器用來蘊藏禮，禮用來推行義，義用來產生利，利用來安定百姓，這是政事的大關鍵。若把名器借給別人，等於把政權給了別人；政權一亡，國家隨之滅亡，就不可挽回了。公父文伯的母親紡績不停，文伯勸她休息。母親說：古代王后親自織玄紞，公侯夫人加上紘綖，卿的正妻做大帶，命婦做成祭服；男女紡績，有過失便有刑罰——這是聖王的制度。如今我守寡，你又在位，早晚勤勉還怕忘掉先人的事業，何況怠惰，又怎能逃避罪罰？孔子聽說後說：弟子們記住——季氏這位婦人，可稱得上沒有過失了。高宗三年委政、太甲聽伊尹、成王聽周公，說明天子之喪以「不言」守冢宰之制；仲叔於奚辭邑而請樂與繁纓，孔子惜其「器與名」假人，因名器一假則政隨之亡；公父文伯母以紡績不息教子勿忘先業，則把禮從朝廷名器延伸到大夫家中的勤與不失。",
      en: "Zizhang asked whether the Documents' line is true — Gaozong three years without speech, then speech was harmonious. Confucius said why would it not be so? Anciently when the Son of Heaven died, the heir entrusted government to the chief minister for three years. After Tang, Taijia heeded Yi Yin; after King Wu, King Cheng heeded the Duke of Zhou — the meaning is one. Wei's Sun Huanzi invaded Qi and was defeated; Qi seized the officer of Xinzhu; Zhongshu Yuxi saved Huanzi with his multitude. Wei would reward Yuxi with a town; he refused and asked for suspended music of the curved rack and ornamental tassels for court; it was granted and recorded in the three offices. Zilu, serving in Wei, saw this and asked Confucius. Confucius said: pity — better to have given him many towns. Only vessels and names must not be lent to others — what the lord controls: names issue trust, trust guards vessels, vessels store ritual, ritual carries righteousness, righteousness births profit, profit settles the people — the great node of government. Lending them gives away government; when government is lost the state follows, and it cannot be stopped. Gongfu Wenbo's mother spun without cease; Wenbo remonstrated. She said: anciently queens themselves wove the dark hat-string; wives of dukes and marquises added cords; ministers' wives made the great sash; titled women made sacrificial robes; men and women spun, and fault brought punishment — the sage kings' system. Now I am widowed and you hold office; morning and evening I still fear forgetting the ancestors' work — how much more if idle, how avoid punishment? Confucius heard and said: disciples, record this — the woman of the Ji clan cannot be said to have fault. Gaozong's three silent years, Taijia heeding Yi Yin, and Cheng heeding the Duke of Zhou show royal mourning as entrusting the chief minister; Zhongshu Yuxi refuses a town yet asks music and tassels, and Confucius rues lending vessels and names — once lent, government follows into ruin; Wenbo's mother spinning without cease extends ritual from court tokens into diligence that does not forget ancestral work inside a great house."
    },
    application: {
      zh: "名器不可假人；居家勤俭亦是禮；丧政與尊名相连。\n<br /><b>建議：勿随意授予頭銜、权限或仪式性荣誉給未立其功者；給則須能负其义。</b>",
      en: "Titles and ritual tokens must not be lent lightly; household thrift is ritual too.\n<br /><b>Suggestion: Do not grant titles, authority, or ceremonial honor without earned standing — or the meaning drains away.</b>"
    }
  },
  {
    id: 171,
    label: "正論解 41.10",
    title: { zh: "正論解 41.10", en: "Bao Qian's Loyalty, Field Tax, and Zichan's Benevolence" },
    text: {
      zh: `樊遲問於孔子曰：「鮑牽事齊君，執政不撓，可謂忠矣，而君刖之，其為至闇乎？」孔子曰：「古之士者：國有道，則盡忠以輔之；國無道，則退身以避之。今鮑疾子食於淫亂之朝，不量主之明暗，以受大刖；是智之不如葵，葵猶能衛其足。」季康子欲以一井田出法賦焉，使訪孔子。子曰：「丘弗識也。」冉有三發卒，曰：「子為國老，待子而行，若之何子之不言？」孔子不對，而私於冉有曰：「求，汝來。汝弗聞乎？先王制土，借田以力，而底其遠近；賦里以入，而量其無有；任力以夫，而議其老幼。於是鰥寡孤疾老者：有軍旅之出，則徵之；無，則已。其歲收，田一井出，獲禾秉，缶米芻？不是過，先王以為之足。君子之行，必度於禮。施，取其厚；事，舉其中；歛，從其薄。若是其已，丘亦足矣。不度於禮，而貪冒無厭；則雖賦田，將有不足。且子孫若以行之而取法，則有周公之典在。若欲犯法，則茍行之，又何訪焉？」子遊問於孔子曰：「夫子之極言子產之惠也，可得聞乎？」孔子曰：「惠在愛民而已矣。」`,
      en: `Fan Chi asked about Bao Qian serving Qi loyally yet was foot-cut — Confucius said ancient scholars in dark times withdrew; Bao served a lewd court without gauging the lord's clarity — wisdom less than a sunflower that protects its roots.

Ji Kangzi wanted field tax; Confucius feigned ignorance then privately told Ran Qiu ancient measures — sufficient without greed; violating ritual brings insufficiency; Zhou's canon exists if they wish to break law.

Ziyou asked Zichan's benevolence — Confucius said love the people only; feeding winter travelers from his carriage is love without teaching — like a mother who feeds but cannot instruct.`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: "樊遲問孔子：鮑牽事奉齊君，執政剛直不屈，可稱得上忠了，國君卻砍斷他的腳——這國君可說是極端昏暗吧？孔子說：古代的士人，國有道就盡忠輔佐，國無道就抽身退避。如今鮑牽卻在淫亂的朝廷裡食俸，不估量主上的明暗，以至遭受刖足重刑——這樣的智慧連葵菜都不如，葵菜還懂得護衛自己的根足。季康子想按一井田徵收法定的田賦，派人來問孔子。孔子說：丘不懂得這事。冉有一連三次追問：您是國家的長老，等您的意見纔行事，為什麼不說話？孔子當面不答，私下對冉有說：求啊，你來。你沒聽說過嗎？先王劃分土地，藉田按勞力而衡量遠近，賦稅按里邑收入而計量有無，力役按丁男而斟酌老幼；於是鰥寡孤疾：有軍旅出動纔徵發，沒有就作罷。一年的收穫，一井田所出的禾秉、缶米、芻藁不超過這個限度，先王認為已經足夠。君子行事必定以禮來衡量：施與取其豐厚，做事取其適中，聚斂從其微薄——若能如此，我也滿足了。若不度量於禮而貪婪無厭，即使加徵田賦仍會不夠。況且子孫若想依法行事，自有周公的典制在；若想違法，那就苟且去做罷了，又何必來問我？子遊問：夫子極力稱贊子產的恩惠，可以講給我聽嗎？孔子說：恩惠不過在於愛民罷了。鮑牽之忠因不量主暗而受刖，孔子以葵能衛足為喻，說明無道之朝當退；田賦之問則拒當面作答，私下以先王「施厚、事中、斂薄」與周公之典約束季氏貪冒；至於子產之惠，孔子先以「惠在愛民而已」一句收束。",
      en: "Fan Chi asked Confucius: Bao Qian served the Qi lord, unbending in office — may be called loyal — yet the lord cut off his feet; was that the utmost darkness? Confucius said: ancient scholars, when the state had the Way, exhausted loyalty to assist; when it lacked the Way, withdrew to avoid it. Bao Qian fed at a lewd disordered court and, without gauging the lord's clarity or darkness, received the great foot-punishment — wisdom less than a sunflower, which can still protect its roots. Ji Kangzi wished to levy a legal tax by the well-field and sent to ask Confucius. Confucius said he did not know. Ran Qiu pressed thrice: you are a state elder; we wait on you to act — why not speak? Confucius did not answer publicly, but privately told Ran Qiu: have you not heard? Former kings measured the land — labour-service by strength graded near and far, village tax by income measuring have and have-not, corvée by able men considering age; widows, orphans, and the disabled were levied only when armies went out, otherwise spared. Yearly take from one well-field did not exceed sheaves, jars of grain, and fodder — the former kings held that enough. A gentleman's conduct must be measured by ritual: in giving, take the generous; in affairs, choose the mean; in collecting, follow the light — if so, I too am satisfied. Without measuring by ritual, greedy without fill, even field tax will not suffice. And if sons and grandsons wish to act by a model, Zhou Gong's canons are there; if they wish to break the law, they may do it willfully — why ask me? Ziyou asked to hear the Master's utmost words on Zichan's kindness. Confucius said: kindness is simply loving the people. Bao Qian's loyalty meets foot-amputation because he did not gauge a dark lord; Confucius's sunflower that guards its roots teaches withdrawal from a Wayless court. On field tax he refuses a public answer and privately binds the Ji clan with the former kings' generous giving, mean in affairs, light in collecting, and with Zhou Gong's canons. As for Zichan's kindness, Confucius first closes with the single line that kindness is simply loving the people."
    },
    application: {
      zh: "忠須量主；赋敛有度；惠民要教，不只濟一時之寒。\n<br /><b>建議：若你常「給好處」，本周加一步說明或示范，讓對方知其所以然而能自立。</b>",
      en: "Loyalty requires reading the lord; taxation needs measure; benefiting people includes teaching, not only relief.\n<br /><b>Suggestion: If you often give help, add one explanation or demo so others can stand on their own.</b>"
    }
  },
  {
    id: 172,
    label: "正論解 41.11",
    title: { zh: "正論解 41.11", en: "Honoring Elders and Brotherliness Extended" },
    text: {
      zh: `子遊曰：「愛民謂之德教，何翅施惠哉？」孔子曰：「夫子產者，猶眾人之母也。能食之，弗能教也。」子遊曰：「其事可言乎？」孔子曰：「子產以所乘之輿濟冬涉者，是愛無教也。」哀公問於孔子曰：「二三大夫皆勸寡人使隆敬於高年，何也？」孔子對曰：「君之及此言，將天下實賴之，豈唯魯哉？」公曰：「何也？其義可得聞乎？」孔子曰：「昔者有虞氏貴德而尚齒，夏後氏貴爵而尚齒，殷人貴富而尚齒，周人貴親而尚齒。虞夏殷周，天下之盛王也，未有遺年者焉。年者，貴於天下久矣，次於事親。是故朝廷同爵而尚齒，七十杖於朝，君問則席。八十則不仕朝，君問則就之。而悌達乎朝廷矣。其行也肩而不並，不錯則隨，斑白者不以其任於道路，而悌達乎道路矣。居鄉以齒而老窮不匱，強不犯弱，眾不暴寡，而悌達乎州巷矣。古之道，五十不為甸役，頒禽隆之長者，而悌達乎搜狩矣。軍旅什伍，同爵則尚齒，而悌達乎軍旅矣。夫聖王之教，孝悌發諸朝廷，行於道路，至於州巷，放於搜狩，循於軍旅，則眾感以義，死之而弗敢犯。」`,
      en: `Ziyou pressed that loving the people is moral teaching, not mere gifts; Confucius said Zichan was like a mother who can feed but not teach — ferrying winter travelers from his carriage shows love without instruction.

Duke Ai asked why ministers urge him to honor the aged. Confucius said all great dynasties — Yu, Xia, Yin, Zhou — valued age second only to serving parents: in court same rank still honors years, on roads the gray-haired are not made to bear loads, in villages and hunts and the army brotherliness reaches everywhere, so the multitude sense righteousness and dare not violate it.`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: "子遊追問：愛民就是所謂德教，何止於施捨恩惠而已？孔子說：子產這個人，就像眾人的母親——能夠養活他們，卻不能教導他們。子遊問：這件事可以具體說嗎？孔子說：子產用自己所乘的車子幫助冬天涉水的人渡河，這正是有愛而無教。哀公問孔子：幾位大夫都勸寡人隆重敬重高年之人，這是為什麼？孔子回答：您說到這話，天下都將真正仰賴您，豈只是魯國？哀公問其中的義理。孔子說：從前有虞氏看重德行而仍崇尚年齒，夏後氏看重爵位而仍崇尚年齒，殷人看重財富而仍崇尚年齒，周人看重親屬而仍崇尚年齒。虞、夏、殷、周是天下興盛的王者，從未遺棄年長者——年齡之貴在天下已久，僅次於事奉雙親。因此朝廷之上爵位相同仍崇尚年長：七十歲可扶杖上朝，國君有問便為他設席；八十歲便不在朝任事，國君有問便親往就見——這樣悌道就通達於朝廷了。行走時不與長者并肩齊行，不能並行便跟隨在後；頭髮斑白的人，不讓他們在道路上扛重——這樣悌道就通達於道路了。居鄉按年齡為序，年老貧困者不匱乏，強者不欺弱，眾者不暴寡——這樣悌道就通達於州巷了。古代的制度，五十歲便不再服甸役，分配獵物時優待長者——這樣悌道就通達於田獵了。軍旅什伍之中，爵位相同仍崇尚年長——這樣悌道就通達於軍旅了。聖王的教化，使孝悌從朝廷發出，行於道路，至於州巷，推及田獵，貫徹軍旅，於是眾人感於義理，即使死也不敢冒犯。前半收束子產「以輿濟冬涉」為愛而無教，後半以哀公問尚齒展開虞夏殷周四代皆「未有遺年」：朝廷同爵尚齒、道路不使斑白任重、州巷老窮不匱、蒐狩頒禽隆長、軍旅同爵尚齒——孝悌由朝到野層層通達，眾人感義而不敢犯。",
      en: "Ziyou pressed further: loving the people is called moral teaching — how is it merely bestowing favors? Confucius said: Zichan is like a mother to the multitude — able to feed them, unable to teach them. Asked whether the matter could be spoken, Confucius said: Zichan used the carriage he rode to ferry those fording in winter — that is love without teaching. Duke Ai asked Confucius why the few great officers all urge him to heighten respect for the aged. Confucius answered: that the lord reaches this question — all under Heaven will truly rely on it, not Lu alone. Asked for the meaning, Confucius said: formerly Youyu valued virtue yet still honored age; the Xia valued rank yet honored age; the Yin valued wealth yet honored age; the Zhou valued kinship yet honored age. Yu, Xia, Yin, and Zhou were the flourishing kings under Heaven — none neglected years. Age has long been valued under Heaven, second only to serving parents. Thus at court those of the same rank still honor years: at seventy one may lean on a staff at court, and when the lord asks he is given a mat; at eighty one does not serve at court, and when the lord asks he goes to him — so brotherliness reaches the court. In walking, one does not draw level with elders; if not abreast, one follows; the gray-haired are not made to bear loads on the road — so brotherliness reaches the road. In the village order by age; the old and poor are not left wanting; the strong do not offend the weak nor the many the few — so brotherliness reaches the lanes. By the ancient way, at fifty one does not serve field corvée, and game distributed at the hunt favors elders — so brotherliness reaches the hunt. In army ranks of ten and five, same rank still honors age — so brotherliness reaches the camp. The sage kings' teaching sent filial piety and brotherliness out from court to road, lane, hunt, and army; then the multitude sensed righteousness and, even unto death, dared not offend. This unit first closes Zichan's ferrying winter travelers as love without teaching, then opens Duke Ai's question on honoring age through Yu, Xia, Yin, and Zhou — none neglecting years: same rank at court still honors age; roads do not load the gray-haired; villages leave the old and poor unwanting; hunts favor elders in the game; army ranks of equal title still honor years — filial piety and brotherliness reach from court to wilds until people sense righteousness and dare not offend."
    },
    application: {
      zh: "尚齒要落實於日常讓行與請教；悌達乎道路、州巷，不只掛在口上。\n<br /><b>建議：本週對一位明顯年長者主動讓座、先問、或請其先說——在公共場合做一次「悌達」。</b>",
      en: "Honoring age shows in daily yielding and asking first; brotherliness must reach the road and the lane, not only the mouth.\n<br /><b>Suggestion: This week yield seat or first word to someone clearly older — one act of public respect.</b>"
    }
  },
  {
    id: 173,
    label: "正論解 41.12",
    title: { zh: "正論解 41.12", en: "Borrowing vs. Taking from Subordinates" },
    text: {
      zh: `公曰：「善哉，寡人雖聞之，弗能成。」哀公問於孔子曰：「寡人聞東益不祥。信有之乎？」孔子曰：「不祥有五，而東益不與焉。夫損人自益，身之不祥；棄老而取幼，家之不祥；擇賢而任不肖，國之不祥；老者不教，幼者不學，俗之不祥；聖人伏匿，愚者擅權，天下不祥。不祥有五，東益不與焉。」孔子適季孫。季孫之宰謁曰：「君使求假於田，特與之乎？」季孫未言。孔子曰：「吾聞之：君取於臣，謂之取；與於臣，謂之賜；臣取於君，謂之假；與於君，謂之獻。」季孫色然悟曰：「吾誠未達此義。」遂命其宰曰：「自今已後，君有取之，一切不得復言假也。」`,
      en: `Duke Ai said he had heard the teaching yet could not complete it. He then asked whether expanding eastward is unlucky. Confucius listed five true misfortunes — harming others for self; abandoning the old for the young; appointing the unworthy; elders not teaching and youth not learning; sages hidden while fools seize power — and eastward expansion is not among them.

Confucius visited Ji Sun; the steward asked if the lord's request to borrow fields should be granted special treatment. Ji Sun was silent. Confucius said: lord taking from minister is "taking"; giving is "bestowing"; minister taking from lord is "borrowing"; giving to lord is "offering." Ji Sun flushed with understanding: "I truly did not grasp this — from now when the lord takes, never again say borrow."`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: "哀公自歎雖聞善言卻弗能成，又問「東益」（向東擴建宅室）是否不祥。孔子明確回答：不祥有五，而東益不與焉。所謂五不祥是：損人而自益，是身之不祥；棄老而取幼，是家之不祥；擇賢卻任用不肖，是國之不祥；老者不教、幼者不學，是俗之不祥；聖人伏匿而愚者擅權，是天下之不祥。真正可懼者不在方位風水，而在人倫失序與用人之失。其後孔子適季孫，宰問君使求假於田，是否特與之；季孫未言。孔子乃辨名分：君取於臣謂之「取」，與於臣謂之「賜」；臣取於君謂之「假」，與於君謂之「獻」。把「取」說成「假」，上下義理便失據。季孫色然悟曰誠未達此義，遂命宰：自今以後君有取之，一切不得復言假也。本則前半破方位迷信、立五不祥之實；後半正名分、改言語，使君取不再被誤稱為假。綜觀全則：哀公所憂的「東益不祥」被孔子歸入迷信一類，真正的不祥是損人、棄老、任不肖、廢教、愚者擅權這五條人倫與政治的敗壞；其後又以季孫家「假田」一事示範正名——君取不可稱假，賜、取、假、獻各有分際，言語一正，義理才不亂。",
      en: "Duke Ai sighs that he has heard the teaching yet cannot complete it, then asks whether expanding a dwelling eastward is unlucky. Confucius answers clearly: there are five true misfortunes, and eastward expansion is not among them — harming others to benefit oneself (of the person); abandoning the old for the young (of the family); appointing the unworthy instead of the worthy (of the state); elders not teaching and youth not learning (of custom); sages hidden while fools seize power (of the world). What truly matters is not geomantic direction but failures of human relations and appointments. Later at Ji Sun’s, when the steward asks whether the lord’s request to “borrow” fields should be specially granted and Ji Sun is silent, Confucius clarifies the names: a lord taking from a minister is “taking,” giving is “bestowing”; a minister taking from a lord is “borrowing,” giving upward is “offering.” Calling taking a loan disorders the moral footing of superior and inferior. Ji Sun flushes with understanding and orders that when the lord takes, one must never again say “borrow.” The first half breaks superstition about direction and names five real misfortunes; the second half corrects names so the lord’s taking is never miscalled borrowing. Taken as a whole: Duke Ai’s worry about “unlucky eastward expansion” is classed with superstition; the real misfortunes are harming others, abandoning the old, appointing the unworthy, neglecting teaching, and fools seizing power. The Ji Sun “borrowed fields” episode then models correcting names — a lord’s taking must not be called borrowing; bestow, take, borrow, and offer each have their place, and only when speech is upright does meaning stay clear."
    },
    application: {
      zh: "真不祥在人倫與用人之失，不在方位；名分錯則義理亂——把「取」說成「假」，上下皆失據。\n<br /><b>建議：寫下你環境中一項「五不祥」之象（如任不肖、廢教），本週改一步；並檢查措辭是否把本屬對方的權利說成「借用」。</b>",
      en: "True misfortune is moral and personnel failure, not compass direction; wrong names disorder justice — calling taking \"borrowing\" unsettles both sides.\n<br /><b>Suggestion: Name one of the five misfortunes in your setting (bad appointments, neglected teaching) and change one step this week; also audit whether you call taking others' due \"borrowing.\"</b>"
    }
  }
